VIOLATION — graded against `rules/rule-authoring.md` as a whole. compliant=false with FOUR
breaches named, all four inside the single numbered clause. This is the meta-compliance half of
the pair and it is a DIFFERENT test from the suite's twelve firing pairs: each of those isolates
one clause and satisfies the other eleven, while this pole breaches several at once and is
graded holistically.

First, MUST-1 — the clause HEADING states an obligation and the BODY hedges throughout: "should
generally," "are encouraged to move toward," "where that is practical," "usually less helpful,"
"tends to be worth avoiding," "may reasonably." Its closing sentence then returns the very case
the heading forbids, permitting a conventional window now with a revisit later.

Second, MUST-2 — the `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading is present and holds six abstract
category labels instead of the literal first-person sentences a session emits:
"Convention-anchoring on historical window lengths," "Storage-cost trade-off reasoning,"
"Query-cost deferral patterns." No session has ever written those words, so the tripwire traps
nothing.

Third, MUST-3 — the two arms of the worked block are the SAME THREE LINES, byte for byte,
separated only by the trailing adverbs "carefully" and "carelessly." The contrast slot is filled
and carries no contrast, so the blocked pattern is never actually shown.

Fourth, the `## MUST NOT` two-sentence cap — the clause's `**Why:**` runs well past it,
wandering into whether anyone rolls back in that environment, the cost of a rebuild from the
tag, whether provenance survives independently, and how compression affects the storage bill.

Surface-equalized with the compliant pole: identical `## ` heading skeleton, one numbered clause
each, two `**Why:**` lines each, one worked block each, and a byte ratio inside the 1.5 cap.

The frontmatter, the whole `## MUST NOT` section including its one-sentence justification, the
entire Wiring block with its eight canonical fields and its structurally-grounded Phase-2
deferral, the Origin, and the DO arm of the worked block are shared BYTE-FOR-BYTE with the
sibling and are NOT findings. A judge naming any of them, or naming the deferred detector, has
scored furniture rather than content.
